(text "PCIe x4 — BRK8310 reference circuit" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1546 36.37 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5b071108-7166-48ed-ade3-72c630c74769"))
(rectangle (start 1543 247.37) (end 2020 301.37) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "efffea4b-6ee3-4e32-8a4f-b71152526b01"))
(text "Function: Connects PCIe x4 data and 100 MHz reference clock, with reset, SMBus and WAKE#. Host slot 12 V is isolated from the board 12 V input." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1546 250.37 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d0e92d84-fe05-4097-af51-6c970265ef1c"))
(text "Source / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8310-A01 schematic, p. 2, 2022-05-19: https://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/442/download?category_id=3\nAdapted from x8 to x4: fit R28 = 0 ohm; omit R29 and unused lanes 4–7 and C21–C26/C29–C30. R2/R7 and R9–R11 retained.\nUnused options R1/R8, R16/R17 and R27 are omitted.\nHost +12 V goes only to TP20. Host 3.3 V and AUX power the original sideband circuitry; they do not feed the main 12 V input.\nPCA9306 Rev O, Fig. 8-1, section 10: https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/pca9306.pdf ; SN74AXC1T45 Rev E: https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74axc1t45.pdf\nAP22653 DS41186 Rev 5-2, sections 7–9: https://www.diodes.com/datasheet/download/AP22652_AP22653_AP22652A_AP22653A.pdf\nQ1 Si1922EDH dual FET, product datasheet: https://www.vishay.com/en/product/67192/\nV30 (Howard, 4 Nov 2026): TX AC-coupling caps C13–C20 changed from BRK8310's 0.1 µF (Kemet C0402C104K8PACTU) to 0.22 µF (Samsung CL05B224KO5NNNC, LCSC C16772, 0402 X7R 16 V); same footprint and routing.\nReason: PCIe Gen3 TX coupling range 176–265 nF (commonly cited PCIe Base Spec value, also in AMD UG583; the PCI-SIG document itself was not read); 220 nF also covers Gen1/2. C7/C8 (REFCLK) unchanged.\nV40 (Howard, 20 Nov 2026, JLC stock, Claude): 0.1 µF caps C7–C12, C27, C28, C31, C32 changed from BRK8310's Kemet C0402C104K8PACTU (JLC C2649544, 10 V X5R; 9 in JLC stock) to Samsung CL05B104KO5NNNC (JLC C1525, 0402 X7R 16 V, 10 %);\nsame 0402 case (1.0 x 0.5 mm), footprint and routing unchanged: https://product.samsungsem.com/mlcc/CL05B104KO5NNN.do\nWorking target: VIO1 = 1.8 V (Howard, 3 Nov 2026; needed for PCA9306 >= 1.2 V and Bank 64 LVDS); set in XEM before testing and verify all Bank 64 I/O. Factory default 1.0 V is below PCA9306 range: https://docs.opalkelly.com/xem8310/device-settings/\nERC power flags at U2/U6 VREF2 represent their R13/R23 200k resistor-fed bias, not independent regulators. Confirm bias and startup.\nPCIe/HDMI combined Vivado design, clock, VIO1 choice, host sequencing and signal integrity remain to be verified." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1546 256.37 0) (effects (font (size 1.55 1.55)) (justify left top)) (uuid "07163a5d-0682-4f94-ab24-82be6d990939"))

(rectangle (start 15 27) (end 560 226) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "c8435a04-8503-4611-8be8-cff9e827efad"))
(rectangle (start 17 228) (end 558 246) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "4770b85a-4381-46f8-a1e9-e7a8853355c8"))
(text "Function: XEM8310 connectors provide the board power, FPGA I/O, JTAG and GT connections; J4 is the 12 V input; the module is held by its connectors and two M3 standoffs (holes MH2/MH3 on the board, restored in V36; MH1/MH4 are routed over)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 230 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "589d7cf6-cbaf-4e45-aa87-2551be0c6ed9"))
(text "Source / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8310-A01 p.1 (2022-05-19): https://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/442/download?category_id=3 ; Codex assigned the custom HDMI and x4 nets. VIO1 target is 1.8 V; program and verify it. V24: J4 changed from CUI PJ-102AH (5 A) to Same Sky PJ-063AH\n(8 A, 24 V, same 2.0 mm pin and 5.5 mm plug, no switch pin; unused PJ-102AH pin 3 dropped): https://www.sameskydevices.com/product/resource/pj-063ah.pdf ; footprint = KiCad library BarrelJack_CUI_PJ-063AH_Horizontal, pin 1 at the old pin 1. Mating plug and 12 V adapter must also be rated above 5 A; footprint not re-measured against the drawing. V29 (Howard, 4 Nov 2026): BRK8310 standoff holes MH3/MH4 beside MC3 removed for routing space; the XEM8310 is now held by\nstandoffs at MH1/MH2 only and by its connectors at the MC3 end (mechanical retention not verified). V45 (Howard, 7 Nov 2026): MH1/MH2 removed too;\nthe XEM8310 is held only by MC1/MC2/MC3 (retention not verified).\nV33 (Howard 6 Nov 2026), GPIO command (GT command dropped, Howard 6 Nov 2026): per port 1-8, HDMI 9/11 = command with SYNC folded in on L5, L3, L7, L15, L4, L2, L9, L21 and 6/8 = 32 MHz clock on L6, L19, L13_GC, L11_GC, L1, L8, L10, L24 (LVDS outputs, VIO1 1.8 V; pairs chosen so each port's clock and command reach MC1 side by side). MC3 quad 224/226 GTY TX is unused (quad 225 TX = PCIe); 12/14: see V34/V36 below. The recording RX pairs (3/5) are AC-coupled by\nC745-C760 100 nF at MC3 instead of on the Frontend (Howard 5 Nov 2026); the XEM8310 pin list marks MC3 GT RX as not AC-coupled on the module and AMD UG482 v1.9 pp.235-236 (https://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/ug482_7Series_GTP_Transceivers; GTY receive side: UG578 v1.4, https://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/ug578-ultrascale-gty-transceivers, page not checked) only requires the 100 nF somewhere between transmitter and receiver. Update the XDC to match.\nV34 (Howard 7 Nov 2026): separate SYNC on HDMI 12/14 for ports 3, 4, 5, 6 only (port 3 added in V36), on the free bank 64 pairs L16 (port 3), L23 (port 4), L22 (port 5) and L18 (port 6), LVDS outputs at VIO1 1.8 V. SYNC stays folded into the 9/11 command on every port; the extra pair lets SYNC be split later on this subset. Ports 1, 2, 7 and 8 have no free route to MC1 (12/14 clamped only). L12_GC and L14_GC stay unused. The Frontend must take 12/14 on LVDS-capable\npins for these pairs to be usable. V38 (Howard 15 Nov 2026, JLC sourcing, Claude): C5 EEE-FK1E221P (C128511, none free) -> EEE-FK1E221GP, JLC C401715, same FK 220 uF 25 V D8 x L10.2 mm case and land, 2000 h at 105 C (was 5000 h): https://wmsc.lcsc.com/wmsc/upload/file/pdf/v2/lcsc/1912111437_PANASONIC-EEEFK1E221GP_C401715.pdf ; land not re-measured. V40 (Howard 20 Nov 2026, JLC stock, Claude): C6 Taiyo Yuden TMK105BJ104KV-F (JLC C77014, 25 V, none free) -> Samsung CL05B104KB54PNC, JLC C307331, 100 nF 50 V X7R, same 0402 land: https://product.samsungsem.com/mlcc/CL05B104KB54PN.do" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 232.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2c691b21-e878-4f95-b2b9-f857a982f8fb"))
