	(rectangle (start 1290 585) (end 1445 680) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "593b471c-53ed-4713-9081-2f6c75c639e0"))
	(text "Function: 2.00 mm header holes for every XEM8310 MC1/MC2 pin this board does not use (Chong via Howard, 7 Nov 2026).\nJ900/J901 + ground row J902 (top-right corner): MC2 banks 84/86/87 and VIO3.\nJ910 + ground row J911 (below MC1): MC1 banks 64/84 with VIO1, VIO2, VREF1, VBATT. J902 pins 1-4 carry I/O and 5-14 are DGND;\nJ911 and the spare pins of J900 (27, 28), J901 (28) and J910 (29) are DGND." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1293 587 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "eb184928-50ce-4614-bef8-19277f40c28e"))
	(text "Source / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8310 breakout, 2.00 mm headers MC4-MC11 (BRK8310-A01 p.1, 2022-05-19:\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/442/download?category_id=3 ; native import ~/kicad_work/brk_ref/BRK8310.PcbDoc).\nNet names = Opal Kelly XEM8310 pin list (https://pins.opalkelly.com/pin_list/XEM8310). Changed from BRK: only the\npins unused here are brought out; Codex chose the header sizes (2x14, 2x15), places and pin order from the board routing;\nP/N pairs are kept next to each other where the routing allowed. V46 (Howard, 7 Nov 2026): bare header holes like BRK8310\nHDR2X20-2MM / HDR1X20-2MM (0.8 mm drill, 1.3 mm pad), no part fitted (not in BOM or placement); every hole is named\non the board silkscreen. Not checked: signal integrity on these lines." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1293 613 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fbb89ef2-e6a3-4ee4-8e42-3e1f9815a0c9"))
	(text "XEM8310 unused-pin header holes (V45; bare holes since V46)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1150 470 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (thickness 0.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "98474fb4-c95a-47b6-812f-f4bc913afd08"))
