	(rectangle (start 1180 699) (end 1312 721.5) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "efaa0648-33f5-498b-bc2a-93a4bec729a0"))
	(text "Function: nine bare test holes for probing the board rails (Chong via Howard, 8 Nov 2026: \"is it difficult to fit these voltage\nheader holes as well?\"). Holes left to right: +1.2V_DDR, VIO1, +1.8V, DGND, +VDCIN (12 V in), DGND, +3.3V, VIO3, VIO2.\nRow below MC1, next to J910/J911; each hole is named on the top and bottom silkscreen. No part fitted (not in BOM or placement)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1182 701 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b9eae91f-7662-46fe-8d4d-c8f715779613"))
	(text "Source / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8310-A01 schematic p.1 (2022-05-19), test points TP1-TP4, TP7, TP8, TP17-TP19 (footprint Aligni:100,\n1.651 mm drill, 2.54 mm pad): https://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/442/download?category_id=3 ; layout = native import of BRK8310.PcbDoc\n(9-hole column at 6.18 mm pitch: DGND, +VDCIN, +1.8V, +3.3V, +1.2V_DDR, VIO1-3, DGND; extra DGND points TP5/TP6 not copied).\nChanged by Claude: one 1x9 footprint J920 at 3.25 mm pitch in a row; order changed so 12 V sits only beside DGND, VIO1 only beside\n<=1.8 V rails, and every feed routes without crossings. 0.2 mm feeds from MC1.2, MC2.1/MC2.69, R2 (+1.2V_DDR), the L4 +3.3V plane,\nJ910.17 and the VIO1 run. Measure only. Not checked: probe/clip fit at 3.25 mm pitch. No series resistors (BRK has none):\na probe slip between neighbours (e.g. +3.3V/VIO3/VIO2, +1.2V_DDR/VIO1) still connects two rails." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 1182 707.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid "067ee8b3-c4e8-446b-9c78-43f27bf071ad"))
